<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#S4.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ 4.2.1 Accuracy of the SPI-BoTER Model in Predicting End-Effector Coordinates ‣ 4.2 Performance on the UR5 Industrial Robot Random Point Dataset ‣ 4 Results and Discussion ‣ SPI-BoTER: Error Compensation for Industrial Robots via Sparse Attention Masking and Hybrid Loss with Spatial-Physical Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>–<a href="#S4.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ 4.2.1 Accuracy of the SPI-BoTER Model in Predicting End-Effector Coordinates ‣ 4.2 Performance on the UR5 Industrial Robot Random Point Dataset ‣ 4 Results and Discussion ‣ SPI-BoTER: Error Compensation for Industrial Robots via Sparse Attention Masking and Hybrid Loss with Spatial-Physical Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> illustrate the scatter plots of predicted versus actual errors for the X, Y and Z axes of the test set. These plots compare the differences between the predicted and theoretical coordinates with those between the measured and theoretical coordinates in the error space, demonstrating that the predicted values closely approximate the measured values. Figure <a href="#S4.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ 4.2.1 Accuracy of the SPI-BoTER Model in Predicting End-Effector Coordinates ‣ 4.2 Performance on the UR5 Industrial Robot Random Point Dataset ‣ 4 Results and Discussion ‣ SPI-BoTER: Error Compensation for Industrial Robots via Sparse Attention Masking and Hybrid Loss with Spatial-Physical Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> presents the error distribution in the test set. The performance metrics summarized in Table <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span> show that the SPI-BoTER model achieves low values for MSE, MAE and RMSE in training, validation and test sets. Except for the Y-axis, the <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> values exceed 0.96, indicating that the model exhibits high accuracy in predicting the coordinates of the end effector of the robotic arm.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.2.2 </span>Performance Comparison between DNN and SPI-BoTER</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This experiment aims to evaluate the effectiveness of the SPI-BoTER framework on the task of predicting the 3D coordinates of an industrial robot end effector. We compared our approach with two baseline methods: the standard Deep Neural Network (DNN) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite> and GPSO-DNN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>. All models were implemented and reproduced on the same random-point dataset of UR robot, consisting of 724 samples. The parameter configurations for both DNN and GPSO-DNN strictly follow those reported in their original publications.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All models were trained under the same hardware environment (NVIDIA RTX A6000 GPU) and consistent training settings, using Adam Optimizer with a learning rate of <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> and a batch size of 256. The comparison of error metrics on the test set is summarized in Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.2.2 Performance Comparison between DNN and SPI-BoTER ‣ 4.2 Performance on the UR5 Industrial Robot Random Point Dataset ‣ 4 Results and Discussion ‣ SPI-BoTER: Error Compensation for Industrial Robots via Sparse Attention Masking and Hybrid Loss with Spatial-Physical Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Figure <a href="#S4.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ 4.2.2 Performance Comparison between DNN and SPI-BoTER ‣ 4.2 Performance on the UR5 Industrial Robot Random Point Dataset ‣ 4 Results and Discussion ‣ SPI-BoTER: Error Compensation for Industrial Robots via Sparse Attention Masking and Hybrid Loss with Spatial-Physical Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> visualizes the performance of the models in the MAE, MSE, RMSE, and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> metrics.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F14" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2506.22788v1/model_comparison.png" id="S4.F14.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/196;" width="286" height="196" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F14.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 14</span>: </span><span id="S4.F14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance Comparison between DNN and SPI-BoTER across MAE, MSE, RMSE, and <math id="S4.F14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Test Set Error Comparison among DNN, GPSO-DNN, and SPI-BoTER</span></figcaption>
<table id="S4.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">Method</th>
